so i have some bad news about apple's  brand new magsafe  wireless chargers and because of this  for me  personally this thing is going to be a  lot less useful than i expected  it might be for you as well now we all  know that because of this new magsafe  charger  the iphone 12s can finally fast charge  wirelessly  at 15 watts which is fantastic  but along with that this supports  standard qi charging so it could support  a variety of devices  just like apple lists on their website  now today this morning it came in  plugged it into my pro display xdr which  has usb  type c and i went ahead and i set down  my iphone 11 pro max on top and it  started charging  like usual this thing's actually not  connected right now but pretend it  started charging up  everything is going just fine now 10  minutes later i go ahead and i pick up  my  phone and to my surprise their  percentage  only went up by two percent and yes  it was aligned perfectly like many of  you out there i'm expecting  7.5 watts out of this charger that's  what multiple tech websites said  and that's a standard for a 10 15 qi  charger  and that's exactly what the iphone 11  pro will accept so out of my curiosity i  went ahead and purchased a well-rated  charging app  and ran one of the many tests that i'm  going to mention  my first result was 2.98  watts now i was expecting 7.5  and at 2.98 that means that it takes  4 minutes to charge this phone by one  percent now at the same time i noticed  a few things the first was that my phone  was already pretty charged so i thought  hmm  maybe it is limiting my wireless  charging because my battery is pretty  well  charged already and the second thing is  you know i'm plugging into my pro  display xdr  maybe it's not able to provide the full  wattage that this new charger needs  it does say on the box that you need a  20 watt usb  type c charger not the 18 watts the new  20 watts so i decided to fix  both of these issues right away i  grabbed a 20 watt  adapter plugged in the new mac save  charger and picked up  my iphone se aligned it perfectly and  started my  test after about 10 minutes i got my  result and it was a shockingly low  1.8 watts now surely this can't be right  this phone can accept 7.5 watts and it's  completely  cool and the battery is almost dead so  it should be able to accept  the whole 7.5 watts from the charger  right that's when i grabbed my really  cheap  charging stand and i'll go ahead and  link this in the description by the way  put my iphone se on top of here and test  it again  and i got a shocking 8.4  watts taking an average of just 39  seconds  for each percentage point gained  compared to three minutes  i gotta say i couldn't believe this so i  tested again  with the magsafe charger making sure  that it is perfectly aligned  and this time i got an even lower 1.49  watts  after this i did a bunch of testing i  grabbed an iphone 10s  i used a different coil to make sure i  also tested out  my note 20 and i took my mophie charger  that apple has been selling  since launch and the results were  interesting  now i don't know about you but i wasn't  only planning to charge my iphone 12  with this charger  i want to replace multiple chargers i  have in my house  with these new ones so i can fast charge  my new iphone 12s  and then at the same time i could toss  my earpods on here i can toss  other devices such as android phones or  older iphones  because these things are so much nicer  sleeker  smaller and better looking i have a few  standard ones  like this mophie so i tested the iphone  se on it  and it got 5.5 watts so just a bit shy  of 7.5  and my iphone 11 pro max got 7.14 watts  despite being pretty well charged over  80  going back to the magsafe charger i  continue to get between  two to three watts charging the iphone  11 pro max with the 20 watt brick  just like i did when it was connected to  my pro display xdr  and no more than two watts on the iphone  se  going as low as 0.96 watts  which is insane my iphone 10s was also  between 1 and 3 watts on magsafe  instead of 7.5 watts next it was time  to test out the note 20 which can accept  15 watt fast charging  but i didn't expect magsafe to offer  that here  since obviously it's designed for the  iphone 12 but i was hoping for  at least 7.5 i couldn't find the same  app but i found one that read the amps  coming in  and instead of getting about 1.3 from my  cheap qi charger  i got about a tenth of that with  constant disconnects  even though it was aligned perfectly  that means that instead of taking  three and a half hours to charge with  seven and a half watts  it would take 13 hours or longer on the  note 20  ultra and between 6 to 12 hours for  iphones  now it's planning to charge a variety of  devices with this magsafe charger  even though i know it won't magnetically  align like it will with the iphone 12  and one of those devices are my earpods  pros  now these things take roughly three  hours to charge  with a cheap qi charger but if you  decide to use  your magsafe charger and it maxes out at  those three watts that i saw  that will take roughly five hours and if  it runs  at just one watt like i saw at times  with the iphone  se that means that it will take 15  hours to charge your earpods compared to  just  two hours plugging them in with a  standard lightning cable  so what did we learn well first off  don't expect  the magsafe charger to give you 7.5  watts of charging  that you typically will use a need for  an iphone 8 or an iphone se  10 10 s 11 all of those devices  or even the five watts that the airpod  pros are designed to work with  i know multiple people have mentioned  this in comments websites are mentioning  this  and that's just what you would expect  because that's what the other iphones  allow and that's what most qi chargers  will give you  i don't know why this is but in reality  we're getting  less than half the wattage from this new  magsafe charger  and at times maybe eight times less  than what i would expect plugging into  one of these devices  and that's a bummer if you were like me  and you wanted to swap a few of your  wireless chargers  to a nice new sleek thin maxi charger so  it takes up less  room and it looks sleeker and that would  give you the ability to have  mag safe for your iphone 12 and you can  fast charge your iphone 12  but then at the same time you can drop  down an android phone  or maybe somebody else in your family  your spouse or your kids  have older iphones that have wireless  charging they can also come in  you know pop it on like that and get  wireless charging as well  well that's not a good idea unless you  really don't like whoever  else is going to be using this charger  and you  want to give them say roughly 6  wireless charging in half hour of charge  time which is  really frustrating you definitely don't  want to replace your other wireless  chargers  or charge other devices and things like  airpods on them  now to point out the apple never said  that this thing can output 7.5 watts  so they're not technically lying about  anything but they are giving us  a list of iphones that are supported  which are all of the wirelessly charging  iphones  so i wish they would disclose how slow  of a charge you're gonna get  if you actually decide to wirelessly  charge those devices  with this new magsafe charger in my  opinion  it really shouldn't be advertised for it  because it is just  too dang slow pretty much useless  let me know your thoughts about these  new mac safe chargers  were you expecting them to put out at  least 7.5  watts if you're spending 40 bucks on the  charger potentially another 20  on a 20 watt usb type-c power brick  i think 7.5 watts is really the standard  these days or even  three four years ago so for me  this is a huge bummer and that means  that i still have to keep  my previous wireless chargers which i  didn't want to do  and that means that the magsafe chargers  are really only useful  for the iphone 12s and at that point  i might as well just keep my lightning  cable there to fast charge that device  and then use the slower wireless  charging for a bunch of other devices or  just for  convenience thank you guys for watching  make sure you guys enable those  notifications because we have a lot of  great iphone 12 and 12 pro videos coming  up by the time you're watching this the  iphones are in our hands  so we have some awesome content that is  in the works thank you guys for watching  click that circle above to subscribe  this has been max and i'll see you in  the next video

